Symbolic & Allegorical Meaning
When read allegorically or as a broader spiritual lesson, the story highlights key contrasts:
Secondhand vs. Genuine Faith: The brothers treat Jesus's name like a magical formula or tool without personal submission or relationship, unlike Paul, whose life and ministry are surrendered to Christ. For a deeper look at this contrast, see Dr. Martyn Lloyd-Jones's sermon.
Borrowed Words vs. Real Authority: Religious titles, family heritage (being sons of a high priest), and borrowed language cannot substitute for authentic spiritual authority.


